## Erosion, landslides, avalanches and earthquakes (server physics goal item 14): an OPTIONAL, SEEDED, BUDGETED terrain-change model.
## PURE: imports only std/math, body (Cell), materials (state classification), blast (BlastResult, the cracked-cell convention).
## No world, entity or server state: the caller hands over a block-state SNAPSHOT (dense box, index = x + nx*(z + nz*y), y slowest,
## the solver's layout) and gets lists back, so a sim can run on a worker thread. Column index c = x + nx*z, cell = c + nx*nz*y.
##
## OUTPUT (drain): CellChange{x,y,z,fromState,toState} (box-local, NET change since the last drain: a cell that moved away and was
## refilled with the same state is not reported), BodyRequest (a coherent slab of >= bodyMinCells cells that left the terrain as one
## rigid mass: spawn it with body.aowl bodyFromCells; the cells are already removed from the box) and EffectEvent (dust/rumble/quake).
## VOLUME IS CONSERVED EXACTLY by landslides and avalanches: every move takes one cell from a column top and puts the same state on
## another column top (or into a BodyRequest). Only snow melt/accumulation and erosion into a body request change the cell count,
## and erosion/landslides themselves never do.
##
## MODEL (a column heightfield H[c] = 1 + y of the highest solid cell; fluid and foliage do not count; overhangs and caves are ignored)
## CLASSES, per state id from materials.materialOf: mcGranular -> granular (dirt, sand, gravel, clay, ...); mcSoft -> soft (only when
##   the run of soft cells on top rests on granular or rock: leaf canopies on logs never slump); the caller's `snowStates` -> snow
##   (handled by the avalanche code only); mcRock -> rock; everything else solid; mcVoid and mcFoliage empty; mcFluid fluid.
## 1 LANDSLIDE. Stability is judged over a span of K = 3 columns (an integer lattice cannot hold a 40 degree slope otherwise):
##   column c is unstable toward a direction when H[c] - min(H[c+d], H[c+2d], H[c+3d]) >= max(2, floor(3 * tanEff) + 1).
##   tanEff = tanRepose * (1 - wetK * wet) - shakeK * shake   (floor 0.05)
##   tanRepose: granular 0.84 (40 deg), soft 1.40 (54 deg). wet 0..1 (per column, from rain: see fillClimate), wetK granular 0.55,
##   soft 0.30 (saturated dirt: 0.38 -> a stable run of <= 1 cell per 3 columns, 18 deg; dry dirt <= 2 per 3: 34 deg).
##   shake = ground acceleration in g (quake + explosion), shakeK 1.0 (the pseudo-static slope stability: tan(phi) - a).
##   The top cell moves to the lowest column of the span (nearest wins). A move needs a drop >= 2, so sum(H^2) strictly falls and the
##   relaxation terminates. Cells never leave the box. Work: a seeded-shuffled dirty-column queue; a move re-queues the 12 columns
##   within 3 of the source and the target. One examination of one column = 1 op; step(sim, budget) stops at the budget.
##   SLABS: before relaxing, mobile-topped columns standing >= slabDiff (3) above a neighbour start a breadth-first cluster of
##   same-height columns up to slabDepth (3) columns inland; the top slabThick (2) cells of a cluster of >= bodyMinCells (32) cells
##   leave as one BodyRequest with a downslope velocity of slabSpeed (0.15) blocks/tick instead of cell by cell.
## 2 AVALANCHE. A snow column (top cells in snowStates, depth >= avalMinDepth 2) with slope tanS = (H[c] - H[c+4d]) / 4 (steepest of
##   4 directions) releases a slab of slabDepth (2) cells when
##       tanS >= avalMinTan (0.45) and tanS * (1 + 0.6 * snowfall) > snowTan * (1 - 0.4 * warm) - snowShakeK * shake   (snowShakeK 1.5)
##   snowTan 0.90 (42 deg), warm = clamp((temp + 5) / 5, 0, 1), snowfall = climate snow 0..1, shake as above (earthquake, explosion
##   triggerExplosion). The released mass is a PACKET walking down the steepest neighbour (with momentum over flats while v > 0.6):
##   v += 0.5 * (drop - 0.30) per column (0.30 = flow friction tan 17 deg), v *= 0.95; it ENTRAINS one snow cell per column from the
##   column it crosses while v >= 0.4 (leaving >= 1 cell, carry <= 96), drops one cell per step when v < 0.3 and the rest at stop
##   (v <= 0, a local minimum, the box edge or 400 steps), each cell on the lowest of the column and its 4 neighbours.
##   Slab steepening re-triggers upslope columns on later scans (retrogressive failure); at most 4096 live packets.
## 3 EROSION (environment pass, ring cursor, `envPerStep` columns per step). Exposed granular tops with rain > 0.05 accumulate
##   erodeRate * dt * rain * (0.2 + steepest drop) cells (default erodeRate 1e-5: 1 cell per ~4 game days of heavy rain on a 45
##   degree bank, "very low"), at >= 1 the top cell is carried down steepest descent (<= 32 columns) and deposited at the first
##   column with no lower neighbour (flats, pits, river beds: a cell may also land in water). Snow: climate snowfall at temp <
##   0.5 adds one snow cell of snowStates[0] per 1/(snowRate*snowfall) ticks (default snowRate 2e-5), temp > 1 melts the top snow cell
##   at meltRate (4e-5 per degree per tick). Both default ON only when snowStates is non-empty and a climate was filled.
## 4 EARTHQUAKES. Quake{x,y,z world epicentre/hypocentre, magnitude, startTick, duration}. Peak ground acceleration in g at 3D
##   distance r: a0(M) = 0.06 exp(0.55 (M - 5)) (M5 0.06, M7 0.18, M8 0.31), a(r) = a0 / (1 + (r / rc)^2), rc = 8 * 10^(0.3 (M - 5))
##   blocks (M7 32). Envelope over the duration: ramp up 15 %, then (1-t)^0.8; +-25 % seeded noise per column per 3 ticks. advance()
##   writes it to the shake field, step() relaxes columns it destabilises and the avalanche scan sees it.
##   quakeCracks(ids, ..., quake, params) -> BlastResult (cracked only), the SAME convention as blast.aowl:
##   applyBlastToSolverInput(inp, result) turns it into weaker solver materials; the caller then re-runs the structural solver.
##   Per cell: a = a(r) * amp * jitter * durF, amp 1.5 when the cell below is empty (decks, overhangs, cantilevers), jitter 0.85..1.15
##   per cell (seeded hash), durF = clamp(0.5 + duration / 400, 0.5, 1.2); fragility wood 1.0, generic 1.2, rock 0.9, others 0
##   (granular and soft ground slump instead). D = frag * clamp((a - 0.05) / 0.10, 0, 1); mult = max(0.05, 1 - 0.9 D), reported when
##   mult <= 0.95. Seeded schedule: quakesInWindow (12000-tick epochs, Gutenberg-Richter b = 1, M = 4.5 + log10(1/u)).
## DETERMINISM: splitmix64 seeded by the seed; ascending iteration; same inputs and seed -> same outputs.

import std/math
import body
import materials
import blast

const
  PkEmpty* = 0
  PkFluid* = 1
  PkGran* = 2
  PkSoft* = 3
  PkSnow* = 4
  PkRock* = 5
  PkSolid* = 6
  SpanK = 3
  SnowSpan = 4

type
  CellChange* = object
    x*, y*, z*: int
    fromState*, toState*: int

  BodyRequest* = object
    ox*, oy*, oz*: int            ## box-local position of the body-local origin (min corner of the cells)
    cells*: seq[Cell]             ## body.Cell, body-local coordinates
    vx*, vy*, vz*: float64        ## initial velocity, blocks/tick
    kind*: int                    ## 0 landslide slab

  EffectKind* = enum efSlump, efAvalanche, efErosion, efQuake, efRumble

  EffectEvent* = object
    kind*: EffectKind
    x*, y*, z*: float64           ## box-local
    intensity*: float64
    count*: int                   ## cells involved

  Quake* = object
    x*, y*, z*: float64           ## WORLD hypocentre
    magnitude*: float64
    startTick*, duration*: int

  ErosionParams* = object
    snowStates*: seq[int]         ## block-state ids that are snow cover (snowStates[0] is placed by accumulation)
    tanGranular*, tanSoft*: float64
    wetKGranular*, wetKSoft*: float64
    shakeK*: float64
    snowShakeK*: float64          ## snow slabs are more shake sensitive than soil
    slabDiff*, slabDepth*, slabThick*, bodyMinCells*: int
    slabSpeed*: float64
    snowTan*, avalMinTan*: float64
    avalMinDepth*, avalSlab*: int
    flowMu*: float64
    maxPackets*: int
    scanPerStep*: int             ## avalanche scan columns per step
    envPerStep*: int              ## environment (erosion, snow) columns per step
    erodeRate*: float64
    snowRate*, meltRate*: float64
    wetDecayTicks*: float64       ## wetness e-folding time after rain stops
    originX*, originY*, originZ*: float64   ## world position of box cell (0,0,0): quakes are in world coordinates

  Packet = object
    x, z, dx, dz: int
    v: float64
    carry: int
    st: int
    life: int

  ErosionSim* = ref object
    nx*, ny*, nz*, nxz*: int
    ids*: seq[int]
    base: seq[int]
    touchedFlag: seq[bool]
    touched: seq[int]
    p*: ErosionParams
    rng: uint64
    seed: int
    tick*: int
    prof: seq[int8]
    top: seq[int]
    wet*, rain*, temp*, snowfall*: seq[float64]
    qa*, ta*: seq[float64]
    acc, sacc, macc: seq[float64]
    lastEnv: seq[int]
    queue: seq[int]
    qhead: int
    inQ: seq[bool]
    quakes*: seq[Quake]
    quakeLive: bool
    scanCursor, envCursor: int
    packets: seq[Packet]
    bodies: seq[BodyRequest]
    evKind: seq[int]
    evCells: seq[int]
    evPos: seq[int]
    slabPending: bool
    climateFilled: bool
    movedCells*: int64
    avalanches*: int
    ops*: int64

  ErosionOutput* = object
    changes*: seq[CellChange]
    bodies*: seq[BodyRequest]
    events*: seq[EffectEvent]

  StepInfo* = object
    ops*: int
    done*: bool          ## no queued work, no live packets (the environment pass is a standing duty and not counted)
    moved*: int

proc defaultErosionParams*(): ErosionParams =
  ErosionParams(snowStates: @[], tanGranular: 0.84, tanSoft: 1.40, wetKGranular: 0.55, wetKSoft: 0.30, shakeK: 1.0, snowShakeK: 1.5,
                slabDiff: 3, slabDepth: 3, slabThick: 2, bodyMinCells: 32, slabSpeed: 0.15,
                snowTan: 0.90, avalMinTan: 0.45, avalMinDepth: 2, avalSlab: 2, flowMu: 0.30, maxPackets: 4096,
                scanPerStep: 512, envPerStep: 256, erodeRate: 1.0e-5, snowRate: 2.0e-5, meltRate: 4.0e-5,
                wetDecayTicks: 6000.0, originX: 0.0, originY: 0.0, originZ: 0.0)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# helpers

proc nextU64(s: var uint64): uint64 =
  s = s + 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15'u64
  var z = s
  z = (z xor (z shr 30)) * 0xBF58476D1CE4E5B9'u64
  z = (z xor (z shr 27)) * 0x94D049BB133111EB'u64
  return z xor (z shr 31)

proc nextF(s: var uint64): float64 = float64(nextU64(s) shr 11) / 9007199254740992.0

proc hashU(seed: int, a, b, c: int): float64 =
  var s = uint64(seed) * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15'u64 + uint64(a) * 0xD1B54A32D192ED03'u64 + uint64(b) * 0x8CB92BA72F3D8DD7'u64 +
          uint64(c) * 0xA0761D6478BD642F'u64
  return nextF(s)

proc clampf(x, lo, hi: float64): float64 =
  if x < lo: return lo
  if x > hi: return hi
  return x

proc kindOfClass(c: MatClass): int =
  case c
  of mcVoid, mcFoliage: PkEmpty
  of mcFluid: PkFluid
  of mcGranular: PkGran
  of mcSoft: PkSoft
  of mcRock: PkRock
  else: PkSolid

proc kindOf(s: ErosionSim, id: int): int =
  if id < 0: return PkEmpty
  if id >= s.prof.len:
    let old = s.prof.len
    s.prof.setLen(id + 1)
    for i in old ..< s.prof.len: s.prof[i] = int8(-1)
  let k = int(s.prof[id])
  if k >= 0: return k
  var r = kindOfClass(materialOf(id).matClass)
  for sn in s.p.snowStates:
    if sn == id: r = PkSnow
  s.prof[id] = int8(r)
  return r

proc cellIdx(s: ErosionSim, c, y: int): int = c + s.nxz * y

proc kindAt(s: ErosionSim, c, y: int): int = kindOf(s, s.ids[c + s.nxz * y])

proc recomputeTop(s: ErosionSim, c: int, fromY: int) =
  var y = fromY
  if y >= s.ny: y = s.ny - 1
  while y >= 0:
    let k = kindAt(s, c, y)
    if k != PkEmpty and k != PkFluid: break
    dec y
  s.top[c] = y + 1

proc touch(s: ErosionSim, i: int) =
  if not s.touchedFlag[i]:
    s.touchedFlag[i] = true
    s.touched.add i

proc putCell(s: ErosionSim, c, y, st: int) =
  let i = c + s.nxz * y
  touch(s, i)
  s.ids[i] = st

proc removeTop(s: ErosionSim, c: int): int =
  let y = s.top[c] - 1
  let st = s.ids[c + s.nxz * y]
  putCell(s, c, y, 0)
  recomputeTop(s, c, y)
  return st

proc placeOn(s: ErosionSim, c, st: int): bool =
  let y = s.top[c]
  if y >= s.ny: return false
  let k = kindAt(s, c, y)
  if k != PkEmpty and k != PkFluid: return false
  putCell(s, c, y, st)
  s.top[c] = y + 1
  return true

proc enqueue(s: ErosionSim, c: int) =
  if c >= 0 and c < s.nxz and not s.inQ[c]:
    s.inQ[c] = true
    s.queue.add c

proc enqueueAround(s: ErosionSim, c: int) =
  let x = c mod s.nx
  let z = c div s.nx
  enqueue(s, c)
  for k in 1 .. SpanK:
    if x - k >= 0: enqueue(s, c - k)
    if x + k < s.nx: enqueue(s, c + k)
    if z - k >= 0: enqueue(s, c - k * s.nx)
    if z + k < s.nz: enqueue(s, c + k * s.nx)

proc evAdd(s: ErosionSim, kind, c, cells: int) =
  # aggregate per 8x8 patch and kind
  let patch = (c mod s.nx) div 8 + ((c div s.nx) div 8) * 1000
  for i in 0 ..< s.evKind.len:
    if s.evKind[i] == kind and s.evPos[i] == patch:
      s.evCells[i] = s.evCells[i] + cells
      return
  s.evKind.add kind
  s.evPos.add patch
  s.evCells.add cells

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# construction

proc newErosionSim*(ids: seq[int], nx, ny, nz: int, seed: int, p: ErosionParams): ErosionSim =
  var s = ErosionSim(nx: nx, ny: ny, nz: nz, nxz: nx * nz, ids: ids, base: ids, p: p, seed: seed, rng: uint64(seed) xor 0x5DEECE66D'u64)
  let n = nx * nz
  s.touchedFlag = newSeq[bool](nx * ny * nz)
  s.touched = @[]
  s.top = newSeq[int](n)
  s.wet = newSeq[float64](n)
  s.rain = newSeq[float64](n)
  s.temp = newSeq[float64](n)
  s.snowfall = newSeq[float64](n)
  s.qa = newSeq[float64](n)
  s.ta = newSeq[float64](n)
  s.acc = newSeq[float64](n)
  s.sacc = newSeq[float64](n)
  s.macc = newSeq[float64](n)
  s.lastEnv = newSeq[int](n)
  s.inQ = newSeq[bool](n)
  s.queue = @[]
  s.prof = @[]
  s.quakes = @[]
  s.packets = @[]
  s.bodies = @[]
  s.slabPending = true
  for c in 0 ..< n:
    s.temp[c] = -5.0
    recomputeTop(s, c, ny - 1)
  # seeded shuffle of the initial dirty list
  var order = newSeq[int](n)
  for c in 0 ..< n: order[c] = c
  var i = n - 1
  while i > 0:
    let j = int(nextU64(s.rng) mod uint64(i + 1))
    let t = order[i]
    let tj = order[j]
    order[i] = tj
    order[j] = t
    dec i
  for c in order: enqueue(s, c)
  return s

proc topKind(s: ErosionSim, c: int): int =
  let h = s.top[c]
  if h <= 0: return PkEmpty
  return kindAt(s, c, h - 1)

proc shakeAt*(s: ErosionSim, c: int): float64 = s.qa[c] + s.ta[c]

## True while a quake is still shaking (the caller keeps stepping).
proc quakeActive*(s: ErosionSim): bool = s.quakeLive

## Is the top cell of column c free to slide, and with which repose tangent.
proc mobileTan(s: ErosionSim, c: int): float64 =
  let h = s.top[c]
  if h <= 0: return -1.0
  let k = kindAt(s, c, h - 1)
  var tn = -1.0
  if k == PkGran:
    tn = s.p.tanGranular * (1.0 - s.p.wetKGranular * s.wet[c])
  elif k == PkSoft:
    var y = h - 1
    var n = 0
    while y >= 0 and kindAt(s, c, y) == PkSoft and n < 8:
      dec y
      inc n
    if y < 0: return -1.0
    let bk = kindAt(s, c, y)
    if bk != PkGran and bk != PkRock: return -1.0
    tn = s.p.tanSoft * (1.0 - s.p.wetKSoft * s.wet[c])
  else:
    return -1.0
  tn = tn - s.p.shakeK * shakeAt(s, c)
  if tn < 0.05: tn = 0.05
  return tn

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# slabs (BodyRequest)

proc dirX(d: int): int =
  if d == 0: return 1
  if d == 1: return -1
  return 0
proc dirZ(d: int): int =
  if d == 2: return 1
  if d == 3: return -1
  return 0

proc neighbour(s: ErosionSim, c, d: int): int =
  let x = c mod s.nx + dirX(d)
  let z = c div s.nx + dirZ(d)
  if x < 0 or x >= s.nx or z < 0 or z >= s.nz: return -1
  return x + s.nx * z

proc cliffAt(s: ErosionSim, c: int): int =
  var best = 0
  for d in 0 .. 3:
    let n = neighbour(s, c, d)
    if n >= 0:
      let df = s.top[c] - s.top[n]
      if df > best: best = df
  return best

proc scanSlabs(s: ErosionSim) =
  if s.p.bodyMinCells <= 0: return
  var seen = newSeq[bool](s.nxz)
  for c0 in 0 ..< s.nxz:
    if seen[c0]: continue
    if mobileTan(s, c0) < 0.0: continue
    if cliffAt(s, c0) < s.p.slabDiff: continue
    # phase 1: the connected run of edge columns (mobile top, cliff >= slabDiff, similar height); phase 2: breadth-first inland
    var cl: seq[int] = @[c0]
    var dist: seq[int] = @[0]
    seen[c0] = true
    var qi = 0
    while qi < cl.len:
      let c = cl[qi]
      inc qi
      for d in 0 .. 3:
        let n = neighbour(s, c, d)
        if n < 0 or seen[n]: continue
        if mobileTan(s, n) < 0.0 or cliffAt(s, n) < s.p.slabDiff: continue
        let dh = s.top[n] - s.top[c0]
        if dh > 1 or dh < -1: continue
        seen[n] = true
        cl.add n
        dist.add 0
    qi = 0
    while qi < cl.len:
      let c = cl[qi]
      let dd = dist[qi]
      inc qi
      if dd >= s.p.slabDepth: continue
      for d in 0 .. 3:
        let n = neighbour(s, c, d)
        if n < 0 or seen[n]: continue
        if mobileTan(s, n) < 0.0: continue
        let dh = s.top[n] - s.top[c0]
        if dh > 1 or dh < -1: continue
        seen[n] = true
        cl.add n
        dist.add dd + 1
    var cellsN = 0
    for c in cl:
      var t = 0
      var y = s.top[c] - 1
      while y >= 0 and t < s.p.slabThick:
        let k = kindAt(s, c, y)
        if k != PkGran and k != PkSoft: break
        inc t
        dec y
      cellsN = cellsN + t
    if cellsN < s.p.bodyMinCells: continue
    # downslope direction: toward the lowest neighbour of the edge columns
    var vx = 0.0
    var vz = 0.0
    var minx = s.nx
    var minz = s.nz
    var miny = s.ny
    for c in cl:
      let x = c mod s.nx
      let z = c div s.nx
      if x < minx: minx = x
      if z < minz: minz = z
      for d in 0 .. 3:
        let n = neighbour(s, c, d)
        if n >= 0 and s.top[c] - s.top[n] >= s.p.slabDiff:
          vx = vx + float64(dirX(d))
          vz = vz + float64(dirZ(d))
      var t2 = 0
      var y2 = s.top[c] - 1
      while y2 >= 0 and t2 < s.p.slabThick:
        let k = kindAt(s, c, y2)
        if k != PkGran and k != PkSoft: break
        inc t2
        dec y2
      if t2 > 0 and y2 + 1 < miny: miny = y2 + 1
    let vl = sqrt(vx * vx + vz * vz)
    if vl > 0.0:
      vx = vx / vl * s.p.slabSpeed
      vz = vz / vl * s.p.slabSpeed
    var br = BodyRequest(ox: minx, oy: miny, oz: minz, cells: @[], vx: vx, vy: 0.0, vz: vz, kind: 0)
    for c in cl:
      var t = 0
      while t < s.p.slabThick:
        let y = s.top[c] - 1
        if y < 0: break
        let k = kindAt(s, c, y)
        if k != PkGran and k != PkSoft: break
        let st = s.ids[c + s.nxz * y]
        br.cells.add Cell(x: int32(c mod s.nx - minx), y: int32(y - miny), z: int32(c div s.nx - minz), state: int32(st))
        discard removeTop(s, c)
        inc t
      enqueueAround(s, c)
    evAdd(s, int(efSlump), c0, br.cells.len)
    s.movedCells = s.movedCells + int64(br.cells.len)
    s.bodies.add br

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# landslide relaxation

proc examine(s: ErosionSim, c: int): bool =
  let tn = mobileTan(s, c)
  if tn < 0.0: return false
  let h = s.top[c]
  var limit = int(floor(tn * float64(SpanK))) + 1
  if limit < 2: limit = 2
  var bestDiff = 0
  var bestT = -1
  var nties = 0
  for d in 0 .. 3:
    let dx = dirX(d)
    let dz = dirZ(d)
    var x = c mod s.nx
    var z = c div s.nx
    var minH = h
    var minC = -1
    for k in 1 .. SpanK:
      x = x + dx
      z = z + dz
      if x < 0 or x >= s.nx or z < 0 or z >= s.nz: break
      let n = x + s.nx * z
      if s.top[n] < minH:
        minH = s.top[n]
        minC = n
    if minC >= 0:
      let df = h - minH
      if df >= limit:
        if df > bestDiff:
          bestDiff = df
          bestT = minC
          nties = 1
        elif df == bestDiff:
          inc nties
          if int(nextU64(s.rng) mod uint64(nties)) == 0: bestT = minC
  if bestT < 0: return false
  # the landing cell must be free
  let ly = s.top[bestT]
  if ly >= s.ny: return false
  let lk = kindAt(s, bestT, ly)
  if lk != PkEmpty and lk != PkFluid: return false
  let st = removeTop(s, c)
  discard placeOn(s, bestT, st)
  inc s.movedCells
  evAdd(s, int(efSlump), c, 1)
  enqueueAround(s, c)
  enqueue(s, bestT)
  return true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# avalanche

proc snowDepth(s: ErosionSim, c: int): int =
  var y = s.top[c] - 1
  var n = 0
  while y >= 0 and kindAt(s, c, y) == PkSnow:
    inc n
    dec y
  return n

proc snowSlope(s: ErosionSim, c: int): (float64, int) =
  # steepest tan over SnowSpan columns in 4 directions and its direction
  let h = s.top[c]
  var best = 0.0
  var bd = -1
  for d in 0 .. 3:
    var x = c mod s.nx
    var z = c div s.nx
    var k = 0
    var last = -1
    while k < SnowSpan:
      let nx2 = x + dirX(d)
      let nz2 = z + dirZ(d)
      if nx2 < 0 or nx2 >= s.nx or nz2 < 0 or nz2 >= s.nz: break
      x = nx2
      z = nz2
      inc k
      last = x + s.nx * z
    if k >= 2:
      let t = float64(h - s.top[last]) / float64(k)
      if t > best:
        best = t
        bd = d
  return (best, bd)

proc scanAvalanche(s: ErosionSim, budget: int): int =
  var used = 0
  var n = budget
  if n > s.nxz: n = s.nxz
  for i in 0 ..< n:
    let c = s.scanCursor
    s.scanCursor = s.scanCursor + 1
    if s.scanCursor >= s.nxz: s.scanCursor = 0
    inc used
    if s.top[c] <= 0 or kindAt(s, c, s.top[c] - 1) != PkSnow: continue
    if s.packets.len >= s.p.maxPackets: continue
    let depth = snowDepth(s, c)
    if depth < s.p.avalMinDepth: continue
    let (tanS, d) = snowSlope(s, c)
    if d < 0 or tanS < s.p.avalMinTan: continue
    let warm = clampf((s.temp[c] + 5.0) / 5.0, 0.0, 1.0)
    let crit = s.p.snowTan * (1.0 - 0.4 * warm) - s.p.snowShakeK * shakeAt(s, c)
    if tanS * (1.0 + 0.6 * s.snowfall[c]) <= crit: continue
    var take = s.p.avalSlab
    if take > depth - 0: take = depth
    var carry = 0
    var st = 0
    for t in 0 ..< take:
      st = removeTop(s, c)
      inc carry
    s.packets.add Packet(x: c mod s.nx, z: c div s.nx, dx: dirX(d), dz: dirZ(d), v: 0.5, carry: carry, st: st, life: 0)
    inc s.avalanches
    evAdd(s, int(efAvalanche), c, carry)
  return used

proc depositOne(s: ErosionSim, c0, st: int) =
  var best = c0
  var bh = s.top[c0]
  for d in 0 .. 3:
    let n = neighbour(s, c0, d)
    if n >= 0 and s.top[n] < bh:
      bh = s.top[n]
      best = n
  if not placeOn(s, best, st):
    if not placeOn(s, c0, st):
      # nowhere to put it: the column is full; drop it on any neighbour that takes it
      for d in 0 .. 3:
        let n = neighbour(s, c0, d)
        if n >= 0 and placeOn(s, n, st): return

proc stepPacket(s: ErosionSim, pk: var Packet): bool =
  ## returns false when the packet is finished (all cells deposited)
  let c = pk.x + s.nx * pk.z
  inc pk.life
  # entrain
  if pk.v >= 0.4 and pk.carry < 96 and s.top[c] > 1 and kindAt(s, c, s.top[c] - 1) == PkSnow and snowDepth(s, c) >= 2:
    let st = removeTop(s, c)
    pk.st = st
    inc pk.carry
  # choose the next column: steepest lower neighbour, or straight on over flats while fast
  var bestD = -1
  var bestDrop = 0
  for d in 0 .. 3:
    let n = neighbour(s, c, d)
    if n < 0: continue
    let drop = s.top[c] - s.top[n]
    if drop > bestDrop:
      bestDrop = drop
      bestD = d
  var sd = -1
  if pk.dx == 1: sd = 0
  elif pk.dx == -1: sd = 1
  elif pk.dz == 1: sd = 2
  else: sd = 3
  if pk.v > 0.6:
    let n = neighbour(s, c, sd)
    if n >= 0 and s.top[n] <= s.top[c] and bestDrop <= 1:
      bestD = sd
      bestDrop = s.top[c] - s.top[n]
  if bestD < 0 or (bestDrop <= 0 and pk.v <= 0.6):
    for i in 0 ..< pk.carry: depositOne(s, c, pk.st)
    evAdd(s, int(efAvalanche), c, pk.carry)
    pk.carry = 0
    return false
  pk.v = (pk.v + 0.5 * (float64(bestDrop) - s.p.flowMu)) * 0.95
  if pk.v <= 0.0 or pk.life > 400:
    for i in 0 ..< pk.carry: depositOne(s, c, pk.st)
    pk.carry = 0
    return false
  if pk.v < 0.3 and pk.carry > 0:
    depositOne(s, c, pk.st)
    dec pk.carry
  pk.dx = dirX(bestD)
  pk.dz = dirZ(bestD)
  pk.x = pk.x + pk.dx
  pk.z = pk.z + pk.dz
  s.movedCells = s.movedCells + 1
  return true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# environment: rain erosion, snow accumulation and melt, wetness

proc lowestNeighbourDrop(s: ErosionSim, c: int): (int, int) =
  var bd = -1
  var bdrop = 0
  for d in 0 .. 3:
    let n = neighbour(s, c, d)
    if n < 0: continue
    let drop = s.top[c] - s.top[n]
    if drop > bdrop:
      bdrop = drop
      bd = d
  return (bd, bdrop)

proc envColumn(s: ErosionSim, c: int) =
  var dt = s.tick - s.lastEnv[c]
  s.lastEnv[c] = s.tick
  if dt <= 0 or s.top[c] <= 0: return
  let k = kindAt(s, c, s.top[c] - 1)
  let fdt = float64(dt)
  if s.rain[c] > 0.05 and k == PkGran and s.p.erodeRate > 0.0:
    let (bd, drop) = lowestNeighbourDrop(s, c)
    s.acc[c] = s.acc[c] + s.p.erodeRate * fdt * s.rain[c] * (0.2 + float64(drop))
    if s.acc[c] >= 1.0:
      s.acc[c] = s.acc[c] - 1.0
      # carry the top cell down steepest descent to the first column without a lower neighbour
      var cur = c
      var steps = 0
      while steps < 32:
        let (d2, dr2) = lowestNeighbourDrop(s, cur)
        if d2 < 0 or dr2 <= 0: break
        cur = neighbour(s, cur, d2)
        inc steps
      if cur != c and s.top[cur] < s.ny:
        let lk = kindAt(s, cur, s.top[cur])
        if lk == PkEmpty or lk == PkFluid:
          let st = removeTop(s, c)
          discard placeOn(s, cur, st)
          inc s.movedCells
          evAdd(s, int(efErosion), c, 1)
          enqueueAround(s, c)
          enqueue(s, cur)
  if s.p.snowStates.len > 0 and s.climateFilled:
    if s.snowfall[c] > 0.02 and s.temp[c] < 0.5 and s.p.snowRate > 0.0 and k != PkFluid:
      s.sacc[c] = s.sacc[c] + s.p.snowRate * fdt * s.snowfall[c]
      if s.sacc[c] >= 1.0:
        s.sacc[c] = s.sacc[c] - 1.0
        discard placeOn(s, c, s.p.snowStates[0])
    elif s.temp[c] > 1.0 and k == PkSnow and s.p.meltRate > 0.0:
      s.macc[c] = s.macc[c] + s.p.meltRate * fdt * (s.temp[c] - 1.0)
      if s.macc[c] >= 1.0:
        s.macc[c] = s.macc[c] - 1.0
        discard removeTop(s, c)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# earthquakes

proc quakePeak*(magnitude: float64): float64 = 0.06 * exp(0.55 * (magnitude - 5.0))
proc quakeRadius*(magnitude: float64): float64 = 8.0 * pow(10.0, 0.3 * (magnitude - 5.0))

## Peak ground acceleration (g) at 3D distance r (blocks).
proc quakeAccel*(magnitude, r: float64): float64 =
  let rc = quakeRadius(magnitude)
  return quakePeak(magnitude) / (1.0 + (r / rc) * (r / rc))

proc quakeEnvelope(t: float64): float64 =
  if t <= 0.0 or t >= 1.0: return 0.0
  if t < 0.15: return t / 0.15
  return pow(1.0 - t, 0.8) / pow(0.85, 0.8)

proc startQuake*(s: ErosionSim, q: Quake) =
  s.quakes.add q
  s.quakeLive = true
  s.slabPending = true
  let c = clampf(q.x - s.p.originX, 0.0, float64(s.nx - 1))
  let cz = clampf(q.z - s.p.originZ, 0.0, float64(s.nz - 1))
  evAdd(s, int(efQuake), int(c) + s.nx * int(cz), 1)

## Explosion or other impulsive trigger: adds a decaying ground acceleration (g) around a box-local point.
proc triggerExplosion*(s: ErosionSim, x, y, z, strength: float64) =
  for c in 0 ..< s.nxz:
    let dx = float64(c mod s.nx) + 0.5 - x
    let dz = float64(c div s.nx) + 0.5 - z
    let a = strength / (1.0 + (dx * dx + dz * dz) / 64.0)
    if a > 0.002: s.ta[c] = s.ta[c] + a
  s.slabPending = true
  for c in 0 ..< s.nxz: enqueue(s, c)

proc advance*(s: ErosionSim, dtTicks: int) =
  s.tick = s.tick + dtTicks
  # decay of impulses
  var anyTa = false
  for c in 0 ..< s.nxz:
    if s.ta[c] > 0.0:
      s.ta[c] = s.ta[c] * pow(0.96, float64(dtTicks))
      if s.ta[c] < 0.002: s.ta[c] = 0.0
      else: anyTa = true
  if s.quakeLive:
    var live = false
    for c in 0 ..< s.nxz: s.qa[c] = 0.0
    for q in s.quakes:
      let t = float64(s.tick - q.startTick) / float64(q.duration)
      if t >= 1.0: continue
      live = true
      let env = quakeEnvelope(t)
      if env <= 0.0: continue
      for c in 0 ..< s.nxz:
        let dx = float64(c mod s.nx) + 0.5 + s.p.originX - q.x
        let dz = float64(c div s.nx) + 0.5 + s.p.originZ - q.z
        let dy = float64(s.top[c]) + s.p.originY - q.y
        let a = quakeAccel(q.magnitude, sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz)) * env
        let nz2 = hashU(s.seed, c, s.tick div 3, 77)
        let v = a * (0.75 + 0.5 * nz2)
        if v > s.qa[c]: s.qa[c] = v
    if live:
      if s.tick mod 4 == 0:
        for c in 0 ..< s.nxz:
          if s.qa[c] > 0.02: enqueue(s, c)
    else:
      s.quakeLive = false
      s.quakes = @[]
  if anyTa and s.tick mod 4 == 0:
    for c in 0 ..< s.nxz:
      if s.ta[c] > 0.02: enqueue(s, c)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# climate coupling

## Fill the per-column weather fields from climate.aowl samples: `sample(wx, wz)` returns (rain, snow, temp) at WORLD column
## (wx, wz) at the surface (the caller wraps climateAt; coarse: every `stride` columns, the others copy the nearest sample).
## Wetness follows rain: wet = max(rain, wet * exp(-dt / wetDecayTicks)).
type ClimateFn* = proc (wx, wz: float64): (float64, float64, float64) {.closure.}

proc fillClimate*(s: ErosionSim, sample: ClimateFn, stride: int, dtTicks: int) =
  var st = stride
  if st < 1: st = 1
  let decay = exp(-float64(dtTicks) / s.p.wetDecayTicks)
  var z = 0
  while z < s.nz:
    var x = 0
    while x < s.nx:
      let (r, sn, t) = sample(float64(x) + 0.5 + s.p.originX, float64(z) + 0.5 + s.p.originZ)
      for zz in z ..< min(z + st, s.nz):
        for xx in x ..< min(x + st, s.nx):
          let c = xx + s.nx * zz
          s.rain[c] = r
          s.snowfall[c] = sn
          s.temp[c] = t
          let w = s.wet[c] * decay
          s.wet[c] = if r > w: r else: w
      x = x + st
    z = z + st
  s.climateFilled = true

proc setUniformWeather*(s: ErosionSim, rain, snowfall, temp, wet: float64) =
  for c in 0 ..< s.nxz:
    s.rain[c] = rain
    s.snowfall[c] = snowfall
    s.temp[c] = temp
    s.wet[c] = wet
  s.climateFilled = true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# the budgeted step

## Do up to `budget` ops (column examinations, avalanche scan columns, packet steps). Standing environment work (rain erosion,
## snow) costs envPerStep columns per call on top of the budget and does not count toward `done`.
proc step*(s: ErosionSim, budget: int): StepInfo =
  var used = 0
  let moved0 = s.movedCells
  if s.slabPending:
    s.slabPending = false
    scanSlabs(s)
    used = used + s.nxz div 4
  # avalanche scan (only when there is snow)
  if s.p.snowStates.len > 0:
    var sb = s.p.scanPerStep
    if sb > budget: sb = budget
    used = used + scanAvalanche(s, sb)
  # packets, one step each per call (a packet in flight advances one column per step: ~20 columns/s)
  if s.packets.len > 0:
    var keep: seq[Packet] = @[]
    for i in 0 ..< s.packets.len:
      var pk = s.packets[i]
      inc used
      if stepPacket(s, pk): keep.add pk
    s.packets = keep
  # landslide relaxation
  while used < budget and s.qhead < s.queue.len:
    let c = s.queue[s.qhead]
    inc s.qhead
    s.inQ[c] = false
    inc used
    discard examine(s, c)
  if s.qhead > 4096 and s.qhead * 2 > s.queue.len:
    var nq: seq[int] = @[]
    for i in s.qhead ..< s.queue.len: nq.add s.queue[i]
    s.queue = nq
    s.qhead = 0
  elif s.qhead >= s.queue.len:
    s.queue.setLen(0)
    s.qhead = 0
  # environment ring
  if s.climateFilled:
    var n = s.p.envPerStep
    if n > s.nxz: n = s.nxz
    for i in 0 ..< n:
      envColumn(s, s.envCursor)
      s.envCursor = s.envCursor + 1
      if s.envCursor >= s.nxz: s.envCursor = 0
  s.ops = s.ops + int64(used)
  let done = s.qhead >= s.queue.len and s.packets.len == 0 and not s.slabPending
  return StepInfo(ops: used, done: done, moved: int(s.movedCells - moved0))

## Run steps until nothing is queued (or maxSteps). Returns the number of steps.
proc relaxAll*(s: ErosionSim, budget, maxSteps: int): int =
  var n = 0
  while n < maxSteps:
    let r = step(s, budget)
    inc n
    if r.done: break
  return n

proc msort(a: var seq[int]) =
  if a.len < 2: return
  var buf = newSeq[int](a.len)
  var w = 1
  while w < a.len:
    var i = 0
    while i < a.len:
      let mid = min(i + w, a.len)
      let hi = min(i + 2 * w, a.len)
      var l = i
      var r = mid
      var k = i
      while l < mid and r < hi:
        if a[l] <= a[r]:
          buf[k] = a[l]
          inc l
        else:
          buf[k] = a[r]
          inc r
        inc k
      while l < mid:
        buf[k] = a[l]
        inc l
        inc k
      while r < hi:
        buf[k] = a[r]
        inc r
        inc k
      i = i + 2 * w
    for j in 0 ..< a.len: a[j] = buf[j]
    w = w * 2

proc drain*(s: ErosionSim): ErosionOutput =
  var o = ErosionOutput(changes: @[], bodies: s.bodies, events: @[])
  s.bodies = @[]
  # touched cells ascending for determinism
  var t = s.touched
  msort(t)
  for i in t:
    s.touchedFlag[i] = false
    if s.ids[i] != s.base[i]:
      let c = i mod s.nxz
      let y = i div s.nxz
      o.changes.add CellChange(x: c mod s.nx, y: y, z: c div s.nx, fromState: s.base[i], toState: s.ids[i])
      s.base[i] = s.ids[i]
  s.touched = @[]
  for i in 0 ..< s.evKind.len:
    let patch = s.evPos[i]
    let px = (patch mod 1000) * 8 + 4
    let pz = (patch div 1000) * 8 + 4
    var kind = efSlump
    if s.evKind[i] == int(efAvalanche): kind = efAvalanche
    elif s.evKind[i] == int(efErosion): kind = efErosion
    elif s.evKind[i] == int(efQuake): kind = efQuake
    let cx = clampf(float64(px), 0.0, float64(s.nx - 1))
    let cz = clampf(float64(pz), 0.0, float64(s.nz - 1))
    let col = int(cx) + s.nx * int(cz)
    o.events.add EffectEvent(kind: kind, x: cx, y: float64(s.top[col]), z: cz, intensity: float64(s.evCells[i]), count: s.evCells[i])
  s.evKind = @[]
  s.evPos = @[]
  s.evCells = @[]
  return o

## Count cells of one state (conservation checks) and the steepest span-3 tangent of the surface (a slope measure for tests).
proc countState*(s: ErosionSim, st: int): int =
  var n = 0
  for v in s.ids:
    if v == st: inc n
  return n

proc columnHeight*(s: ErosionSim, x, z: int): int = s.top[x + s.nx * z]

proc maxSpanSlope*(s: ErosionSim): float64 =
  var best = 0.0
  for c in 0 ..< s.nxz:
    for d in 0 .. 3:
      var x = c mod s.nx
      var z = c div s.nx
      for k in 1 .. SpanK:
        x = x + dirX(d)
        z = z + dirZ(d)
        if x < 0 or x >= s.nx or z < 0 or z >= s.nz: break
        let t = float64(s.top[c] - s.top[x + s.nx * z]) / float64(k)
        if t > best: best = t
  return best

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# earthquake damage: strength multipliers for the structural solver

proc fragilityOf(c: MatClass): float64 =
  case c
  of mcWood: 1.0
  of mcGeneric: 1.2
  of mcRock: 0.9
  else: 0.0

## ids: snapshot box nx*ny*nz (solver layout). q is in the box's own coordinates here (the caller subtracts the box origin), so
## the same call works for any box. Returns a BlastResult holding only `cracked` (ascending cell index), directly usable with
## applyBlastToSolverInput. `seed` varies the per-cell jitter.
proc quakeCracks*(ids: seq[int], nx, ny, nz: int, q: Quake, seed: int): BlastResult =
  var r = BlastResult(destroyed: @[], cracked: @[], debris: @[], impulses: @[], ops: 0, done: true)
  let durF = clampf(0.5 + float64(q.duration) / 400.0, 0.5, 1.2)
  # early out: nearest point of the box
  let nxp = clampf(q.x, 0.0, float64(nx))
  let nyp = clampf(q.y, 0.0, float64(ny))
  let nzp = clampf(q.z, 0.0, float64(nz))
  let dmin = sqrt((nxp - q.x) * (nxp - q.x) + (nyp - q.y) * (nyp - q.y) + (nzp - q.z) * (nzp - q.z))
  if quakeAccel(q.magnitude, dmin) * 1.5 * 1.15 * durF <= 0.05: return r
  var known: seq[int] = @[]
  var fr: seq[float64] = @[]
  let nxz = nx * nz
  for i in 0 ..< nx * ny * nz:
    let sid = ids[i]
    if sid == 0: continue
    var f = -1.0
    for k in 0 ..< known.len:
      if known[k] == sid:
        f = fr[k]
        break
    if f < 0.0:
      f = fragilityOf(materialOf(sid).matClass)
      known.add sid
      fr.add f
    if f <= 0.0: continue
    let c = i mod nxz
    let y = i div nxz
    let x = c mod nx
    let z = c div nx
    let dx = float64(x) + 0.5 - q.x
    let dy = float64(y) + 0.5 - q.y
    let dz = float64(z) + 0.5 - q.z
    var amp = 1.0
    if y > 0 and ids[i - nxz] == 0: amp = 1.5
    let jit = 0.85 + 0.30 * hashU(seed, i, 5, 9)
    let a = quakeAccel(q.magnitude, sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz)) * amp * jit * durF
    if a <= 0.05: continue
    let d = f * clampf((a - 0.05) / 0.10, 0.0, 1.0)
    var mult = 1.0 - 0.9 * d
    if mult < 0.05: mult = 0.05
    if mult <= 0.95:
      r.cracked.add CrackedCell(cell: i, mult: mult)
  return r

## Seeded quake schedule: epochs of 12000 ticks, each holds a quake with probability `chance` (default use 0.02; 0 = none).
## Epicentre uniform in [wx0, wx1) x [wz0, wz1), hypocentre `depth` blocks below baseY, M = 4.5 + log10(1/u) (b = 1, >= 7 in 0.3 %).
proc quakesInWindow*(seed: int, tick0, tick1: int, wx0, wz0, wx1, wz1, baseY, chance: float64): seq[Quake] =
  var res: seq[Quake] = @[]
  if chance <= 0.0 or tick1 <= tick0: return res
  var e = tick0 div 12000
  if tick0 < 0 and e * 12000 != tick0: e = e - 1
  while e * 12000 < tick1:
    if hashU(seed, e, 1, 1) < chance:
      let st = e * 12000 + int(hashU(seed, e, 2, 1) * 12000.0)
      if st >= tick0 and st < tick1:
        var u = hashU(seed, e, 3, 1)
        if u < 1.0e-6: u = 1.0e-6
        var m = 4.5 + log10(1.0 / u)
        if m > 9.0: m = 9.0
        res.add Quake(x: wx0 + (wx1 - wx0) * hashU(seed, e, 4, 1), y: baseY - 5.0 - 10.0 * hashU(seed, e, 5, 1),
                      z: wz0 + (wz1 - wz0) * hashU(seed, e, 6, 1), magnitude: m, startTick: st,
                      duration: 100 + int(60.0 * (m - 4.0)))
    inc e
  return res
